counterfactuals.output:
**An automotive thermal management system comprising:**

a heat-transfer medium circuit configured to circulate a heat-transfer medium;

a first heat source comprising an electric traction motor and configured to transfer waste heat to the heat-transfer medium through a first heat-source flow path;

a second heat source comprising a traction battery and configured to transfer waste heat to the heat-transfer medium through a second heat-source flow path;

a first heat generator comprising an internal-combustion engine and configured to supply generated heat to the heat-transfer medium through a first heat-generator flow path;

a second heat generator comprising an electric coolant heater and configured to supply generated heat to the heat-transfer medium through a second heat-generator flow path;

a thermal load comprising at least one of a passenger-compartment heat exchanger, a battery heat exchanger, or a refrigerant-to-coolant heat exchanger; and

a valve assembly fluidly coupled to the first and second heat-source flow paths, the first and second heat-generator flow paths, and the thermal load, the valve assembly being selectively operable between a plurality of switching states to:  
(i) fluidly connect the first heat-source flow path to the thermal load;  
(ii) fluidly connect the second heat-source flow path to the thermal load;  
(iii) fluidly connect at least one of the first or second heat-generator flow paths to the thermal load; and  
(iv) isolate or bypass one or more of the respective flow paths.

A controller is operatively coupled to the valve assembly and configured to select one of the plurality of switching states based on at least one of an ambient temperature, a passenger-compartment heating demand, a temperature of the traction battery, a temperature of the electric traction motor, or an operating state of the internal-combustion engine, thereby selectively recovering waste heat, supplying actively generated heat, or combining waste heat and actively generated heat to regulate a temperature of the thermal load.
